# Line endings: pin everything to LF.
#
# `zig fmt --check` is a required gate and it depends on LF. Without this file,
# Git's default `core.autocrlf=true` on Windows rewrites line endings in the
# working copy on checkout, so the gate fails on files nobody edited - a
# confusing way to learn about a checkout setting.
#
# `eol=lf` for text files keeps the working tree byte-identical across platforms;
# binary assets are excluded explicitly.
* text=auto eol=lf

*.pem binary
*.der binary
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.svg text eol=lf
